  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">for Ghana Cities Monitor: Measuring and Ranking the Quality of Governance and Service Provision</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Center for Democratic Development (CDD-Ghana) is a nonpartisan, nongovernmental, not-for-profit research and policy advocacy think tank working to promote democracy, good governance, and inclusive development in Ghana and Africa. With this grant, CDD-Ghana will continue the implementation of the Ghana Cities Monitor &#x2014; an index designed to assess, monitor, and report periodically on service delivery and provision of public goods in major Ghanaian cities based on the quality of governance and the provision of goods and services. (Strategy: Inclusive Governance)</narrative>
  </description>
